    "section": "5 Clearances, separations, and spacings",
    "page": 41,
    "text": "For wires or conductors carrying currents greater than 1/3 of, but not exceeding, their rated ampacity, the design conductor temperature for the thermal loading condition shall be a) calculated in accordance with ANSI/IEEE 738 for the anticipated worst-case conditions; or b) 100 °C for bare conductors and 80 °C for covered conductors.",
