    "text": "structures Where suspension insulators that are not restrained from swinging transversely are used, sufficient clearances between the live end of an insulator string in a swing-out position and the supporting structure shall be maintained. The following conditions shall be considered to determine the required structure head geometry to accommodate swinging insulator string: a) high wind with power frequency voltage — operational requirement; b) moderate wind with switching surge overvoltage — operational requirement; and c) low wind with switching surge overvoltage — live-line maintenance requirement (where applicable).",
