    "section": "5 Clearances, separations, and spacings",
    "page": 43,
    "text": "There is no vertical separation requirement for communication terminals, supply switch handles, and control, police, and fire-alarm boxes, provided that they are effectively grounded and do not obstruct pedestrian traffic.",
    "tablesReferenced": [],
