    "text": "circuits The minimum in-span vertical clearance between supply-line conductors of different circuits of the same or different voltage classes and attached to the same supporting structure shall be as specified in Table 21, and shall apply under the following conditions: a) the upper conductor shall be assumed to be at maximum sag; and b) the lower conductor shall be assumed to be at initial unloaded sag at the mean annual temperature.",
