    "page": 61,
    "text": "poles, metal structures, towers, and guys The assumed transverse load for wood, concrete, and fibre-reinforced composite poles, metal structures, towers, and guys shall be calculated by multiplying the transverse loads specified in Clause 7.6.2 by the appropriate transverse load factors in Tables 31 and 32. For guyed wood or concrete poles, the pole at the point of guy attachment shall be designed to withstand the total assumed loads.",
