    "title": "8 Strength of supporting systems according to deterministic design — Clause 8.12.2.1",
    "section": "8 Strength of supporting systems according to deterministic design",
    "page": 72,
    "text": "Communication drops or cables without supporting messengers shall not be used a) in proximity to or crossing over supply lines greater than 750 V line-to-ground; or b) in spans longer than 30 m in heavy and severe loading areas, or spans longer than 38 m in medium loading areas. Note: Item (b) applies to communication drops only.",
    "tablesReferenced": [],
    "crossReferences": [],
