    "title": "Grounding conductor",
    "section": "9 Grounding methods for supply systems less than or equal to 22 kV and",
    "page": 79,
    "text": "The grounding conductor shall be made of copper or another metal or combination of metals that will not corrode excessively during the expected service life of the conductor under existing conditions. Where joints are unavoidable, they shall be made and maintained such that they do not materially increase the resistance of the grounding conductor and they shall have appropriate mechanical and corrosion-resistant characteristics.",
