    "section": "9 Grounding methods for supply systems less than or equal to 22 kV and",
    "page": 79,
    "text": "On communication-only lines, the support strand shall be grounded at each end of the pole line and at intervals not exceeding 1200 m. No point on the cable sheath shall be further than 600 m from a ground. The cable sheath bonding interval shall not exceed a) 300 m for copper cables; and b) 1500 m for fibre cables.",
