    "section": "Annex A (informative)",
    "page": 139,
    "text": "Experience has shown that ice tends to collect on the down-wind side of the pole and thus does not add to the cross-sectional area upon which the wind acts. In addition, ice on the pole tends to lower the drag coefficient. In essence ice on the structure is not a governing case.",
